How to apply it

Open your License.md file.
Delete everything currently in it.
Copy everything between the ===LICENSE_START=== and ===LICENSE_END=== lines.
Remove the two === marker lines.
Paste the text and save.

This keeps the repo fully GPLv3 (as shown in the README) while still offering a path for commercial use — exactly what we had before.
Would you like me to also update the README’s Licensing section to point to this new License.md cleanly? Or is this enough for now?3.6sexcellejnt and waht was "Version 3, 29 June 2007" again?Quick answer:
"Version 3, 29 June 2007" is the official title and release date of the GNU General Public License version 3 (GPLv3).
It is the standard legal header that appears at the top of every official GPLv3 license text. You should keep it exactly as written — it is not something you change.
Correct full header (copy-paste ready):
MarkdownGNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE
Version 3, 29 June 2007
That’s all it is — just the formal name + date of the license. It’s required for the license to be legally valid and recognizable.
So in your License.md, leave that line exactly as I gave it to you. It’s correct and standard.3.2s
